#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
shopee - agent-native BUYER CLI for Shopee Taiwan (shopee.tw, TWD). No checkout.
Zero dependencies (Python 3.8+ stdlib). Every command supports --json and
returns the {ok, data|error} envelope used by the other ~/Projects shop CLIs.
Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 api, 2 usage, 3 auth, 4 net/blocked (incl. Shopee anti-bot).

Transport, measured 2026-10-30 against the user's real Edge on CDP 9222
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Plain HTTPS to /api/v4/search/search_items (browser UA, Referer) ->
    HTTP 403 {"error":90309999,...,"9":true}: Shopee's anti-bot code for an
    unsigned request. The web app's own calls carry af-ac-enc-dat,
    af-ac-enc-sz-token, x-sap-ri, x-sap-sec, x-sz-sdk-version, d-nonptcha-sync
    (all minted in-page by the anti-fraud SDK).
  * fetch() from inside a shopee.tw tab -> same 90309999 (the SDK does not
    hook fetch).
  * XMLHttpRequest from inside a shopee.tw tab -> the SDK DOES hook XHR and
    adds the signed headers itself; measured 200 with data, but only about 1
    in 3 attempts (others 90309999), even 8 s after page load, and 0/3 for
    cart/add_to_cart. Used only by `raw` (and whoami --via browser).
  * Loading the real page in a background tab and reading the page's OWN API
    response (CDP Network.getResponseBody) -> 200 with data on ~20 loads in a
    row. This is the read transport: search page -> /api/v4/search/search_items,
    product page -> /api/v4/pdp/get_pc, cart page -> /api/v4/cart/get. Later
    (after ~40 requests in ~45 min, 9-25 s apart) even the search page's own
    search_items came back as the 1.2 kB 90309999 refusal (5 loads, 12:18-12:33),
    while the cart page still loaded - so 90309999 means "stop for a while"
    no matter which transport.
  * Rate: an HTML "429 Too Many Requests" page came back after ~12 page loads
    + ~8 XHRs in ~10 minutes. The CLI paces requests (SHOPEE_MIN_INTERVAL,
    default 9 s, shared across processes) and caches each Shopee result page
    for 10 minutes (SHOPEE_CACHE_TTL) so paging/sorting re-uses data.
  * Guests (signed out): search page=N is rewritten to page=0, and product
    pages redirect to /verify/traffic/error?...is_logged_in=false&type=4 with
    get_pc -> 90309999. A captcha (/verify/captcha?scene=crawler_item) was
    shown once after ~9 guest page loads/XHRs. Everything here assumes Edge is
    signed in on shopee.tw; the CLI never solves captchas or types passwords.

Endpoints (the page's own requests unless noted)
------------------------------------------------
Search  GET /api/v4/search/search_items?by=<relevancy|price|sales|ctime>
            &keyword=<q>&limit=60&newest=<page*60>&order=<asc|desc>
            &page_type=search&scenario=PAGE_GLOBAL_SEARCH&source=SRP&version=2
        issued by https://shopee.tw/search?keyword=<q>[&sortBy=price&order=asc][&page=N]
        (signed in: page=N honoured -> newest=N*60, 60 items). Two item
        shapes were seen: item_basic{price,price_min,price_max,
        price_min_before_discount,...} (XHR) and item_data{item_card_display_price
        {price,strikethrough_price,applied_product_promo_price,original_price,
        recommended_shop_voucher_info}} + item_card_displayed_asset{name,...}
        (the page's own request). Measured 60/60 items:
        applied_product_promo_price == item_basic.price_min.
        Prices are integers = TWD x 100000.
        Ads: search_item_tracking JSON has is_ads / item_type_str ("organic");
        adsid/campaignid set on ad slots. 32 of 60 raw results on a signed-in
        relevance page were ads (dropped).
        PRICE BASIS: `price` = the lowest variant's current price (price_min,
        after product promotions, before vouchers). The search card's own
        number (`card_price`) can be lower because Shopee subtracts a
        recommended shop voucher (measured: NT$3 item shown as NT$0 after a
        NT$3 voucher with min spend 0); it is reported but never sorted on.
        Shopee's own price sort orders by that card number, so for
        --sort price/price-desc the CLI pools Shopee's first
        PRICE_POOL_PAGES x 60 price-sorted results, drops ads/hidden prices,
        dedupes by (shopid,itemid) and re-sorts by `price` - so the order is
        monotonic, but only within that pool (ceiling documented).
        Relevance: Shopee reorders its own page 0 between calls (measured:
        page-1/page-2 overlap 1/10 without caching), hence the result-page
        cache plus a per-query memory of ids already shown on earlier pages.
        Placeholders: listings priced exactly NT$99,999 are dropped - both seen
        were gift-only ("<贈品專用，請勿自行下單！>", "加價購 [完全贈品]").
        NT$1-3 listings are real (checked: 【活動用】 NT$1 = one single pack,
        orig NT$10, shipping NT$45-165) and are kept.
Product GET /api/v4/pdp/get_pc?item_id=&shop_id=&tz_offset_in_minutes=480&detail_level=0
        issued by https://shopee.tw/product/<shopid>/<itemid>. data.item: title,
        brand, price_min/price_max (+ _before_discount), raw_discount, stock
        (null; stock_display "尚有庫存"), tier_variations[{name,options}],
        models[{model_id,name,price,price_before_discount,has_stock,
        extinfo.tier_index}]; data.product_price.price.single_value = the
        voucher-applied 券後價 when has_final_price (measured 995 -> 915, shop
        voucher YFYSN1080 NT$80 off >= NT$800); data.shop_detailed{name,
        is_official_shop}; data.product_shipping.ungrouped_channel_infos[].name
        and shipping_fee_info.price; data.product_review{rating_star,
        total_rating_count}. Search price_min == product price_min (995 == 995).
Account GET /api/v4/account/basic/get_account_info -> data{userid, username,
        nickname, email, phone, shopid}. Works over PLAIN HTTPS with the saved
        cookies (measured), so login/whoami need no browser.
Cart    POST /api/v4/cart/get  body {"pre_selected_item_list":[],
        "updated_time_filter":{"start_time":0},"cart_state":{},
        "version_list":[3787143115,1023]} (issued by https://shopee.tw/cart).
        data.cart_block_id_list[].item_briefs = EVERY line (shopid, itemid,
        modelid, quantity; measured 47) but data.cart_blocks[].items details
        (name, model_name, price, stock, status, checkout) only for the first
        pagination_info.item_limit = 20. The page loads the rest on scroll via
        an observer that does not fire in a hidden tab (8 scrolls: nothing).
        POST /api/v4/cart/add_to_cart {quantity, checkout:false,
        update_checkout_only:false, donot_add_quantity:false, source:"",
        shopid, itemid, modelid}  and  POST /api/v4/cart/update
        {action_type: 1 EDIT_QUANTITY | 2 DELETE, updated_shop_order_ids:[{shopid,
        item_briefs:[{shopid,itemid,modelid,item_group_id,add_on_deal_id,
        is_add_on_sub_item,quantity,old_modelid,old_quantity,checkout,
        applied_promotion_id,price}]}], selected_shop_order_ids, promotion_data,
        cart_state, version_list} - shapes taken from the public cart/PDP JS
        bundles on deo.shopeemobile.com, NOT from a captured live write.
        MEASURED 2026-10-30: add_to_cart via the signed in-page XHR was refused
        3/3 times (90309999); the re-read cart was unchanged each time. Driving
        the real buttons was declined (account risk: it is also a seller shop),
        so `cart add/qty/rm` refuse up front with exit 2 and make no request.
        update (qty/rm) was never attempted live.

Rate limits and pacing (built in)
---------------------------------
  * >= SHOPEE_MIN_INTERVAL seconds (default 9) between Shopee requests across
    all `shopee` processes (timestamp ~/.config/shopee/.last_request).
  * Any 429 / 90309999 / captcha / traffic-verify -> exit 4, no retry, and a
    cool-down (~/.config/shopee/.cooldown_until: 10 min, 3 min for 90309999)
    that makes every later call refuse to send anything until it expires.
  * Multi-request commands (price with several ids, uncached price-sorted
    pools) print the number of requests and expected wait to stderr first.

Login: never passwords/OTP. `shopee login` copies shopee.tw cookies (not
seller.shopee.tw) from Edge on SHOPEE_CDP; if Edge is signed out it opens
https://shopee.tw/buyer/login in a background tab and waits (--wait 300) for
you. Saved to ~/.config/shopee/state.json (0600) or keyring; SHOPEE_COOKIE
overrides. SPC_U = numeric user id when signed in, "-" when signed out
(SPC_EC is "-" even when signed in - not a logout signal).

No checkout / order / payment endpoint is ever called (cart/checkout exists in
the bundle and is deliberately not used).

Unofficial, undocumented private API; it can break without warning. Shopee
bans automation aggressively; this account may also be a seller shop.
"""
